{"title":"Career Roadmap · Cartographer","role":"Cartographer","summary":"A Cartographer creates, analyses, maintains and communicates geographic information through maps and other geospatial visualisations.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Geography & Environmental Planning"},"about":[{"label":"Degree Alignment","text":"Excellent"},{"label":"Primary Sectors","text":"GIS, Mapping, Urban Planning, Surveying, Environmental Consulting, Government, Defence, Transportation, Infrastructure"},{"label":"Typical Entry Roles","text":"GIS Technician, Junior Cartographer, Mapping Analyst, GIS Analyst, Geospatial Technician"},{"label":"Long-Term Roles","text":"Cartographer → Senior Cartographer → GIS Specialist → Geospatial Lead → GIS/Mapping Manager"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Cartographer creates, analyses, maintains and communicates geographic information through maps and other geospatial visualisations."},{"type":"p","text":"Modern cartography is no longer limited to drawing physical maps. It combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Geography","GIS","Remote Sensing","Data","Visualisation","Programming"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"A graduate in Geography & Environmental Planning has a strong academic foundation because the degree develops knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physical geography"},{"text":"Human geography"},{"text":"Environmental systems"},{"text":"Spatial relationships"},{"text":"Land use"},{"text":"Urbanisation"},{"text":"Regional planning"},{"text":"Population"},{"text":"Natural resources"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should add strong GIS and digital mapping skills to become professionally competitive."},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"A BA can lead directly to junior GIS/cartography roles, but specialist cartographer, GIS consultant, remote-sensing and advanced geospatial roles often prefer a postgraduate qualification or substantial technical experience."}]},{"heading":"What Does a Cartographer Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A modern cartographer typically works with geographic datasets and converts them into accurate, useful visual products."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical responsibilities"},{"type":"table","header":["Area","Work"],"rows":[[{"text":"Map creation"},{"text":"Design physical and digital maps"}],[{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Manage and analyse spatial data"}],[{"text":"Data processing"},{"text":"Clean and transform geographic datasets"}],[{"text":"Spatial analysis"},{"text":"Identify geographic patterns"}],[{"text":"Remote sensing"},{"text":"Analyse satellite/aerial imagery"}],[{"text":"Thematic mapping"},{"text":"Create population, climate, land-use etc. maps"}],[{"text":"Web mapping"},{"text":"Build interactive online maps"}],[{"text":"3D mapping"},{"text":"Create terrain/city visualisations"}],[{"text":"Survey data"},{"text":"Integrate GPS/GNSS and survey information"}],[{"text":"Urban planning"},{"text":"Produce planning maps"}],[{"text":"Environmental mapping"},{"text":"Map ecosystems, pollution and land cover"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Maintain spatial databases and metadata"}]]}]},{"heading":"Career Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"During BA"},{"text":"GIS Intern, Mapping Intern, Geospatial Intern"}],[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"GIS Technician, Junior Cartographer, Mapping Technician, GIS Assistant"}],[{"text":"1–4 years"},{"text":"Cartographer, GIS Analyst, Mapping Analyst, Geospatial Analyst"}],[{"text":"3–7 years"},{"text":"Senior Cartographer, GIS Specialist, Remote Sensing Analyst"}],[{"text":"6–10 years"},{"text":"Geospatial Consultant, GIS Lead, Senior GIS Specialist"}],[{"text":"10+ years"},{"text":"GIS Manager, Geospatial Programme Lead, Mapping/Geospatial Director"}]]}]},{"heading":"Build Skills During the BA","kind":"other","